WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.639 align:start position:19%
Half a million books gone in a single
night. Not stolen, not hidden, burned to

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:14.639 align:start position:19%
ash while the greatest minds on earth
watched helpless. This is the story of

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:19.920 align:start position:19%
the greatest library ever built and the
day humanity's memory went up in flames.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:24.480 align:start position:19%
I am standing on the cornes of
Alexandria, Egypt, watching fishing

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:30.400 align:start position:19%
boats rock in the same harbor where
warships once docked.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:35.760 align:start position:19%
rises a giant tilted disc of glass and
granite. The new Library of Alexandria

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:41.440 align:start position:19%
opened in 2002.
The building it honors, that one

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.440 align:start position:19%
vanished 2,000 years ago.

